        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm trying to place नट in the dhatupatha lists — checking whether it belongs to the churadi \"नट अवस्पन्दने\" entry versus the bhvadi \"नट नृत्तौ\" (ghaṭādi mit) form, and whether it carries the iṭ marker alongside entries like ज्ञप.\n\nStill recalling more churadi roots...\n\nI'm continuing to recall more root verb groups from this grammatical list, trying to place where this particular sequence of dhatus belongs among the classical groupings.\n\nI'm continuing through this list of Sanskrit verbal roots with their meanings, moving through entries like चर्च, बुक्क, शब्द, कण, जभि, and many others covering senses of study, speech, breaking, binding, and ornamentation.\n\nI'm continuing through this list of dhatu roots with their meanings, and recalling that \"नट\" meaning \"अवस्पन्दने\" appears in the churadi class per Kshiratarangini and Kashika, forming \"नाटयति.\"\n\nSince only ज्ञपादि verbs carry mit status in non-causal churadi, नट doesn't qualify, so the causal form stays नाटयति, giving लङ् प्रथम बहुवचन as अनाटयन्.\n\n",
